Patch 03: service and person cards link to their object nodes, so tap opens ObjectOverlay (src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx)

Rationale: SiteClient already intercepts clicks on a[href^="/o/"]
and opens ObjectOverlay (node projection: identity, evidence-backed
summary, facts, contact, provenance, related objects, ask entry),
restoring scroll on close. But nothing on the tenant site currently
links to /o/, so the overlay is unreachable. This patch makes
service and person section cards link their titles to /o/<objectId>,
giving mobile visitors (and desktop users) tap-to-node object depth
with zero new chrome: no floating button, no drawer, no explorer.

Binding compliance:
- Modifier clicks (new tab) and #ask links pass through unchanged
  (existing interceptor behavior in site-client.tsx).
- The overlay stays a single-object sheet; related objects render
  as peer-jump links, never as a browseable grid. It must not
  become the All Objects explorer through the back door.
- Ask entry routes to the ONE assistant with {siteId, objectId}
  context (existing askHref in object-overlay.tsx).

Verified seam: renderSection cases "Services" and "People" dispatch
to ServicesSection and PeopleSection (renderer.tsx, read 2026-09-23).
Exact card markup inside those section components was NOT read; the
hunk below is placed at the documented seam and marked where
implementation must read the card body.

Proposed change (apply inside ServicesSection and PeopleSection
card render; read each card body first):

  --- a/src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx
  +++ b/src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx
  @@ ServicesSection card (exact lines TBD at implementation)
  -        <h3>{object.title}</h3>
  +        <h3>
  +          <a href={`/o/${encodeURIComponent(object.id)}`}>{object.title}</a>
  +        </h3>
  @@ PeopleSection card (exact lines TBD at implementation)
  -        <h3>{object.title}</h3>
  +        <h3>
  +          <a href={`/o/${encodeURIComponent(object.id)}`}>{object.title}</a>
  +        </h3>

Alternative (lower risk, same outcome): wrap the whole card in the
anchor only if the card has no other interactive children; title
link is preferred because it preserves existing card actions.

Acceptance: tapping a service card opens ObjectOverlay with the
object's evidence-backed node projection; close returns to the exact
scroll position; the overlay's ask entry routes to /o/<id>#ask with
siteId; no /o/ links leak for objects absent from the public graph
(the interceptor already guards on graph membership).
